---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Projects" description="Projects by Elliot Nelson.">
	<h1>Projects</h1>

	<h2>LadderJS</h2>
	<p>
		A JavaScript recreation of the 1982 CP/M game "Ladder", a game I played for
		countless hours on a Kaypro II when I was much younger.
	</p>
	<p>
		Check out the <a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/ladderjs"
			>GitHub repo</a
		> or <a href="https://ladderjs.7tonshark.com/">try it in your browser</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>js13k Game Projects</h2>

	<h3>Ashes of Ulthar (2025)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2025-ashes-of-ulthar"
			>Ashes of Ulthar</a
		> was my 2025 entry for #js13k. A gloomy race-against-the-clock pixel art resource
		simulator. See the <a href="/posts/making-of-js13k-2025-ashes-of-ulthar/"
			>post-jam write-up</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h3>Harold is Heavy (2023)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2023-harold-is-heavy"
			>Harold is Heavy</a
		> was my 2023 entry for #js13k. A silly, colorful platformer. See the <a
			href="/posts/making-of-js13k-2023-harold-is-heavy/">post-jam write-up</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h3>Moth (2022)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2022-moth">Moth</a> was my 2022
		entry for #js13k, with blocky pixel art and a clearly defined palette. See the <a
			href="/posts/making-of-js13k-2022-moth/">post-jam write-up</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h3>Shadow of the Keening Star (2021)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2021-keening-star"
			>Shadow of the Keening Star</a
		> was my 2021 entry for #js13k. A short ASCII roguelike plus text-based adventure
		game that turned out surprisingly compelling once it all came together.
	</p>

	<h3>WIZARD WITH A SHOTGUN (2020)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2020-wizard-with-a-shotgun"
			>WIZARD WITH A SHOTGUN</a
		> was my 2020 entry for #js13k. A top-down 2D pixel art shooter — sound, music,
		a little dialog and story — and probably the closest I've gotten to a complete
		game.
	</p>

	<h3>Letchworth Village (2019)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2019-letchworth-village"
			>Letchworth Village</a
		> was my 2019 entry for #js13k. Shipped half-finished for lack of time, but I still
		enjoy the aesthetic. Written in TypeScript, which was an interesting experiment.
	</p>

	<h3>Raven (2018)</h3>
	<p>
		<a href="https://github.com/elliot-nelson/js13k-2018-raven">Raven</a> was my 2018
		entry for #js13k. A top-down 2D stealth game involving a lot of raycasting math —
		a fun way to dust off stuff I loved working on years ago.
	</p>
</Base>
